    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495-a1">

                <pb facs="0575" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg495"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <p>His Majesty’s Government have received information from the officer administering
                    the government of Ceylon that 10 prisoners of war of American nationality are
                    still there, being unable to defray the cost of their passage home.</p>
                <p>In these circumstances, His Majesty’s Government desire to ascertain whether the
                    United States Government wish to let them remain to await their turn to be sent
                    home or to make any special arrangements for their conveyance.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
